# Test: IS-IS top-level config validation (spec-isis-4 component/config wiring).
#
# VALIDATES: spec-isis-4-component-config -- a top-level `isis { ... }` block
#            reaches the IS-IS component's config schema and validators: a valid
#            NET (and the per-interface metric/hello/circuit-type/level leaves)
#            validate through the real YANG schema and the custom NET validator
#            (User Story 1, AC-1/AC-2), while a structurally invalid NET (bad
#            length / NSEL) is rejected by the isis-net custom validator before
#            the engine mutates state (User Story 2, AC-3/AC-4).
# PREVENTS:  regression where the `isis` config root is not wired (validate
#            passes vacuously) or the NET validator is not registered (an invalid
#            NET is silently accepted).
#
# Live adjacency / LSDB / SPF behaviour needs raw L2 (AF_PACKET) on a Linux veth
# and is covered by the QEMU integration tests and the sibling specs
# (isis-5/6/7/9); this functional test exercises the config wiring only:
# config file -> YANG schema -> NET/system-id validation.

# --- Valid config: a full isis block validates. -----------------------------
stdin=isis-valid:terminator=EOF_VALID
isis {
	net 49.0001.0000.0000.0001.00
	level l1-l2
	lsp-lifetime 1200
	hostname r1
	interfaces {
		interface eth0 {
			metric 10
			hello-interval 10
			hold-multiplier 3
			priority 64
			circuit-type point-to-point
			level l1-l2
		}
		interface eth1 {
			passive true
		}
	}
}
EOF_VALID

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze config validate -:stdin=isis-valid:exit=0
expect=exit:code=0
expect=stdout:contains=configuration valid

# --- Invalid NET: wrong length / NSEL is rejected. ---------------------------
stdin=isis-bad-net:terminator=EOF_BAD
isis {
	net 49.0001.00
}
EOF_BAD

cmd=foreground:seq=2:exec=ze config validate -:stdin=isis-bad-net:exit=1
expect=exit:code=1
